# TSRX / Octane Components

## Component shape

```tsrx
import { useState } from 'octane';

export function MyComponent(props: { title: string }) @{
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);

  <section class="my-component">
    <h2>{props.title as string}</h2>
    @if (open) {
      <p>Expanded</p>
    }
  </section>
}
```

## Rules

- Use `@{ ... }` body shorthand; one JSX root per component — **no `return` inside `@{}`**
- Dynamic text: `{expr as string}` when type is not provably string
- Control flow: `@if`, `@for (item of list; key item.id)`, `@try` / `@pending` / `@catch`
- Use `class`, not `className`; native events (`onClick`, `onInput`) — no synthetic `onChange` on text inputs
- Refs are props: `ref={myRef}`

## Hooks in `.ts` modules

Custom hooks shared across components go in `.ts` files with the Octane ownership pragma:

```ts
/** @jsxImportSource octane */
import { useState } from 'octane';
```

## Pages vs components

- **Pages** (`src/pages/`) — file-based routes; add a lowercase `.tsrx` file to create a route (see **octane-pages** rule)
- **Components** (`src/components/`) — reusable UI
- **UI fields** (`src/ui/ContentFields/`) — CMS `Section` / `Field` / `ImageField` / etc.
- **Context** (`src/context/`) — theme; avoid putting CMS fetch logic here

## Async CMS data in TSRX

Wrap PatStore hooks in `@try` / `@pending` / `@catch` — see `src/content/Home/components/CmsArticles.tsrx`:

```tsrx
@try {
  const items = usePatStoreCollection('Article', { limit: 6 });
  <ul>...</ul>
} @pending {
  <p>Loading…</p>
} @catch (_e) {
  <p>Could not load content.</p>
}
```
